# MVO Scope And Stubbing

The first MVO is the LinkSites / WebsiteFactory lead-to-preview-site flow.

The demo must show:

- lead selection/import
- template selection
- copy generation
- preview site generation/publishing
- CRM record or accepted CRM stub
- Plane project/tasks or accepted Plane stub
- LiNKbot mission execution
- LinkSkills capability lease/run
- LiNKautowork deterministic workflow run
- LiNKbrain event/audit/memory write
- LiNKaios trace/status view

If a third-party integration blocks the 7-day compression target, create a documented MVO stub and continue.

Acceptable stubs:

- seed CSV instead of live lead provider
- local CRM table instead of Chatwoot/Odoo
- local project/task table instead of Plane
- static/local preview instead of full hosted publishing
- simplified policy response if the capability lease is still recorded

Unacceptable stubs:

- no audit event
- no capability lease
- no memory/event write
- no trace/status visibility
- fake success without proof
